<title>USA: FOCUS-ARCO, Thrifty deal seen hiking retail prices.</title>
<headline>FOCUS-ARCO, Thrifty deal seen hiking retail prices.</headline>
<byline>David Brinkerhoff</byline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Motorists in southern California will see higher prices for retail gasoline following Atlantic Richfield Co's takeover of the state's last large independent chain, industry observers say.</p>
<p>ARCO, a leading gasoline seller with 18 percent market share in the state, agreed Monday to operate over 260 stations owned by Thrifty Oil Co. The deal's terms were not disclosed.</p>
